# PoolP8-2 (lane PoolP8, 2026-10-30): a request whose pictures have more feature rows than startup set aside for the
# tower (engine.vision_rows_reserved: 16,384 + the workspace past its base / 8 KiB) gets a LazyVisionFeed: before
# each of its prompt chunks is decided or sent, rank 0 encodes the pictures the chunk reads (multi._encode_ahead)
# and drops the ones the prefill is past, so at most one chunk's pictures are held instead of every row before
# the ADMIT. Same rows (the tower encodes each picture on its own), ids, replies. A tower failure fails that request
# alone, as the eager path does at admission: its client gets the tower's error, FINISH frees its slot and rows,
# the states its own prefill kept are evicted (not one it resumed from); image prompts are never in a shared chunk.
# With it TENSORFOLD_VISION_WORKSPACE_MIB=768 serves the 102,400-token picture budget without the 1,440 MiB
# reservation, so the P8 pool is production's.
